{"availability":"available","full":"muazzezwq/CallGuard","name":"CallGuard","description":"On-chain SLA marketplace for machine-to-machine API calls, on Arc Testnet","category":"Developer tools","language":"HTML","stars":1,"forks":0,"created":"2026-04-19T19:32:01Z","updated":"2026-10-08T20:45:23Z","branch":"main","homepage":"https://arcsla.vercel.app","topics":[],"demo":"https://arcsla.vercel.app/app/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T23:43:16.680Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-08T23:43:16.680Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-08T23:43:16.680Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-08T23:43:16.680Z","stars":1,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Programmable service settlement for autonomous services — built on Arc.","Providers stake USDC and commit to a response-time SLA. Callers pay per request and get a signed receipt. Miss the deadline and the stake is slashed automatically — no court, no arbiter, no middleman.","Built on Arc Testnet, Circle's stablecoin-native L1 where USDC is the native gas token. Every interaction — call, receipt, slash — costs a fraction of a cent and settles in under a second."],"features":["Provider stakes USDC as a performance bond","Caller pays per request — USDC goes into escrow","Provider signs an EIP-712 receipt after delivery — escrow releases","If the provider misses the SLA window, anyone can trigger a slash — caller gets a refund plus a bonus from the stake"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/muazzezwq/CallGuard/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"5519e6dfa40e27288234ab17a9b9d3db4588adbdb3aa78b79c215d1a9b5bcdb0","extractedAt":"2026-10-08T23:43:16.854Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T23:43:16.854Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Programmable service settlement for autonomous services — built on Arc.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/muazzezwq/CallGuard/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"Onboard